From 1cd69ad890496e4c7fec33e231433521e2693c8e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 03:32:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] docs: document the new CI gates and the Kubernetes
 deployment

README gains a Kubernetes section: apply order, what the network
policies allow and what they break (in-cluster callers must go through
the gateway), how to enable the inventory and a launcher (ConfigMap,
pod IP as advertise host, the instance port policy), a GPU-free trial
with the fake launcher, and what vllm-process would need on Kubernetes
including its single-node limitation. The common commands list gains
make coverage and make audit.

CONTRIBUTING documents the coverage floor (only ever raised), the
fresh-virtualenv import check and the Go version CI uses. The
CHANGELOG and the module mapping describe the package import check,
the dependency audit, the coverage floor, Go 1.27, the new manifests
and their manual validation on kind; the network policies are marked
as breaking.
